  "implementation": "Subdivide original active control polygons when two nonzero control edges have a dot product below -64*machine-epsilon after normalization. Recursively trim halves with existing exact producers, reusing usd-brep in native command builds. Evaluate each clamped single-span leaf on [0,1], avoiding unrepresentable source-chart derivatives, and map sample tags to the original source chart. Default outline intervals are 64+2*order, rounded up to a multiple of density+1. Draw density+1 hair intervals per leaf while all differential stations contribute to the outline and extraction. Reuse the existing curvature evaluator, singular-gap behavior, seam welding, immutable cache and display-scale checks. Bound aggregate stations to 200000 and subdivision depth to 32. Keep the uniform geometry API for other clients.",
  "inference": "The default-density outline count follows degree and rounds to a multiple of hair-density+1 in the tested curves. The control-cone heuristic reproduces many observed adaptive grids, but three additional source curves disprove complete native subdivision equivalence. The setting SampleDensity is documented publicly; requests to change it continued to report 2 in these native captures. No alternative outline-density control is exposed locally based on those unsuccessful requests.",
